    "clinical_benefit": "unknown",
    "engine_predicts_patients": "unknown"
  },
  "cannot_know": "This channel measures allele fractions in bulk specimens and lower bounds on the fraction of tumour cells carrying a variant. It is NOT a clonal reconstruction: two variants at the same lower bound may sit in the same cells or in different cells, and nothing here resolves that. It carries no copy number, no purity, no treatment record and no outcome, so it cannot say whether a change was caused by therapy, by sampling or by drift, and it cannot be scored as the engine's clone state. A rising variant is a measurement, not a prediction.",
  "limitations": [
    "a DECLARED gene panel, not the whole variant space: the mutations endpoint of this profile requires a gene filter",
    "no purity and no copy number are carried, so only a lower bound on the clone fraction is published",
    "specimens are labelled by KIND, not by day, so 'primary versus recurrence' is the only pairing and no day-0/day-N mapping exists",
    "no treatment record and no outcome is joined to these specimens",
    "the panel is genome-filtered by gene, so a change in a gene outside it is invisible here"
  ]
}